<title>USA: Conn seen selling $260 mln of bonds in Aug 11 week.</title>
<headline>Conn seen selling $260 mln of bonds in Aug 11 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Connecticut plans to sell in the week of  Aug 11 around $260 million of new money, general obligation bonds  through PaineWebber, a financial market source said Friday.</p>
<p>The source, who declined to be named, said this was the state's regular  autumn sale of such bonds.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Connecticut treasurer did not have all the details  of the offering immediately available.</p>
<p>((--Joan Gralla, 212-859-1654))</p>
